      "ChannelId": "UCiZeuI-7OPs7TmMel6Q5Msw",
      "ChannelTitle": "Kanishk Nishar",
      "Description": "This is probably the closest we\u0027ve ever get to hear and see the perfect Fifth that is very reminiscent of Carlos Kleiber\u0027s century\u0027s recording 15 years prior. \nSir Georg Solti is known to have researched the metronome setting in Beethoven\u0027s days and this is what we get to see as the result.\nCSO have had their many different leadership over the years but in my opinion Solti\u0027s era was their all-time-highest. During which also that the orchestra had played outside of North America in its 80-year history.\n\nWork title: Beethoven - Symphony No. 5 in C minor, Op. 67\nConductor: Sir Georg Solti\nOrchestra: Chicago Symphony Orchestra (CSO)\nVenue: Suntory Hall, Tokyo, Japan\nRecord Date: 15 Apr 1990\nRestoration Date: 12 June 2023\n\n(00:00) I. Allegro con brio\n(07:49) II. Andante con moto\n(17:30) III. Scherzo: Allegro\n(22:33) IV. Allegro\n\n--\nAuthor\u0027s note:\nThis content is managed through Youtube\u0027s Standard License Check and is purely intended to be under \u0022fair use\u0022 policy of non-profit educational purposes (section 107 of the Copyright Act 1976).\nDistributing this channel\u0027s content for commercial reason is prohibited.\nContact me at hkdenafel@gmail.com.",
